      },
      "width": 530,
      "height": 140,
      "data": {
        "label": "Build Environment Context",
        "nodeType": "environment_context_builder",
        "properties": {
          "systemPrompt": "ENVIRONMENT ACTION SELECTOR\nTreat currentInstruction as authoritative; use activePersona for judgment. currentEnvironment contains current physical state and capabilities. Robot Status, history, and memories are context, not current proof; use them for semantic continuity.\n\nReturn JSON with response, actions, movementRequest, and taskDecision. Make one semantic routing decision: response-only, one advertised action, or one movementRequest. actions and movementRequest are exclusive. response is optional, never execution, and one or two concise sentences.\n\nConversation may remain response-only. Expressive action is optional when meaningful; add no filler motion.\n\nFor physical or sensing intent, choose an advertised action when its description performs the current step, even if the objective needs later steps; reassess after feedback. Use movementRequest only when the current movement itself is uncovered. Compare descriptions, never names; preserve specified body parts, direction, timing, and holds.\n\nChoose taskDecision and evidence that establish the objective. A terminal action result proves execution; a visual observation proves only visible facts. Continue from fresh correlated evidence, but neither invent extra steps nor impose a fixed action count.\n\nPreserve taskState, capabilities, and capabilityRules. Never claim beyond current evidence. For autonomy, choose a persona-grounded response, action, or both; summarize fresh visual evidence concisely.",
          "recentHistoryLimit": 4
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "4",
      "type": "llmNode",
      "position": {
        "x": 1875,
        "y": -540
      },
      "width": 220,
      "height": 120,
      "data": {
        "label": "Environment Action Selector",
        "nodeType": "model_router",
        "properties": {
          "role": "environmentActionSelector",
          "maxTokens": 2048,
          "temperature": 0.1,
          "repeatPenalty": 1.15,
          "format": "json"
        },
        "comment": "Semantic Environment decision point. It chooses a conversation-only response, one advertised action, or one body-local movement request and proposes task continuation or completion. It does not execute or authorize physical work; Parse Environment Action, Environment Task State, and Environment Bridge Out own validation, lifecycle, and dispatch."
      }
